step Rough Grinding Stone to 83
  tip Rough Grinding Stone is green at 75 (yellow 45, green 65, grey 85): about 58 crafts to 83. Each takes 2 Rough Stone. Two Rough Stone a craft. Grinding stones are parts for later plans; the extras sell to vendors. If you got here without learning Rough Grinding Stone, learn it now: an earlier step teaches it.
  learn 3320
  craft 3320 until 83

step Runed Copper Belt to 100
  tip Runed Copper Belt is orange at 83 (yellow 85, green 105, grey 125): about 21 crafts to 100. Each takes 10 Copper Bar. Forever teaches Runed Copper Belt from 45; it stays orange to 85. Ten Copper Bars a craft: smelt your Copper Ore. Needs an anvil nearby. Blacksmith Hammer is a tool: keep it in your bags.
  craft 2666 until 100

step Blacksmithing recipes at 100
  tip Back to a Blacksmithing trainer: Heavy Sharpening Stone (from 100, 10s).
  learn 2674

step Heavy Sharpening Stone to 113
  tip Heavy Sharpening Stone is yellow at 100 (yellow 100, green 107, grey 115): about 28 crafts to 113. Each takes 1 Heavy Stone. Heavy Stone comes from Iron Deposits; one a craft.
  craft 2674 until 113

step Blacksmithing recipes at 113
  tip Back to a Blacksmithing trainer: Patterned Bronze Bracers (from 95, 5s).
  learn 2672

step Patterned Bronze Bracers to 150
  tip Patterned Bronze Bracers is orange at 113 (yellow 125, green 140, grey 155): about 64 crafts to 150. Each takes 5 Bronze Bar and 2 Coarse Grinding Stone. Make the 128 Coarse Grinding Stone first. Each bracer takes two Coarse Grinding Stones (Coarse Stone from Tin Veins): make them first; they give points too. Needs an anvil nearby. Blacksmithing 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3326 x128
  craft 2672 until 150
  skill Blacksmithing 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert (150-225)
section Blacksmithing 150-225

step Expert Blacksmithing
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225 for 50s (Classic's price; Forever's is not in the data); it needs Blacksmithing 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Bengus Deepforge (Ironforge); Horde Saru Steelfury (Orgrimmar). The arrow picks the nearest of your faction. Learn now: Green Iron Bracers (from 140) and Heavy Grinding Stone (from 100, 10s). 150-225 takes about 10s of recipes and 28s of vendor goods, plus 234 Heavy Stone, 168 Iron Bar, 195 Steel Bar, 320 Mithril Bar and 30 Solid Stone to gather or buy.
  level 20
  train Blacksmithing Expert
  learn 3501
  learn 3337

step Blacksmithing 150-225: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 28 Green Dye (28s); about 28s in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Alexandra Bolero, Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Borya, Felika and Shimra). If you smelt the 195 Steel Bar yourself (Mining 165: an Iron Bar and a Coal each), buy 195 Coal too (9g 75s, trade and blacksmithing suppliers); skip them if you buy the bars.
  buy 2605 x28 nearest
  buy 3857 x195 nearest optional

